From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-08-21
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] basicswap: fund a chain-A swap lock only from
 non-malleable inputs, and stop misrouting p2pkh wallet funds

PATCH-3/4/6 let the electrum wallet hold and spend a legacy (P2PKH) BTC/LTC
derivation. Auditing the funding and swap-lock path for the same gap turned
up three separate hardwired-segwit assumptions in interface/btc/btc.py's
_fundTxElectrum, plus one in electrumx.py and one in basicswap.py's own
"needs consolidating" heuristic. All five are fixed here.

1. THE PROTOCOL-SAFETY ONE. BasicSwap pre-signs the chain-A lock's refund
   against the lock TRANSACTION'S OWN predicted txid -- createSCLockRefundTx
   hashes the unsigned funded tx before either party has broadcast anything
   (basicswap.py, unpatched: tx_lock.rehash(); tx_lock_id_int = tx_lock.sha256).
   A witness input's signature lives outside that hash and can't move it; a
   legacy P2PKH input's signature lives INSIDE it (scriptSig), so signing
   such an input changes the txid the refund was bound to. Upstream already
   fails closed for this -- sendXmrBidCoinALockTx raises "Coin A lock tx
   txid changed after signing!" -- but only after the counterparty has
   already exchanged refund signatures, with no indication that the
   wallet's OWN address type caused it. And nothing upstream actually
   filters which UTXOs are eligible to fund a lock tx; the RPC-mode fundTx
   even carries the upstream comment "# TODO: Manually select only segwit
   prevouts", unimplemented.

   fundTx/_fundTxElectrum gain require_segwit_inputs (default False, so
   ordinary withdrawals are untouched); fundSCLockTx sets it. A legacy-only
   wallet now refuses funding a swap lock with a clear, early error --
   before any message reaches a counterparty -- rather than silently
   building a lock tx that either dies at broadcast or trips upstream's own
   late guard after the other side has already committed.

2. THE FEE ONE. The same function priced every selected input as a fixed
   68 vB (P2WPKH-sized) and every change output as P2WPKH regardless of the
   change address's real encoding. A legacy P2PKH input is ~148 vB (no
   witness discount) -- underpriced by more than half. This was already
   live the moment address_type shipped in PATCH-3, for every funded
   transaction including ordinary sends, not just the swap path this patch
   otherwise concerns. Vsize is now priced per UTXO by its own address
   encoding (matching PATCH-6's actual per-input signing branch: a legacy
   input's dummy witness entry is now empty too, mirroring the real signer
   leaving no witness data for it), and legacy scriptSig bytes are costed
   through getTxVSize's add_bytes channel rather than folded into the
   witness-only add_witness_bytes.

3. THE SILENT-MISROUTE ONE. The change output was built via
   decodeAddress()+getScriptForPubkeyHash(), which always emits a P2WPKH
   script -- even when change_addr is a p2pkh address string. A p2pkh
   wallet's change would land on a script its own address table never
   derives or subscribes to: not lost (the key is known, so it is
   technically recoverable by hand), but invisible to the wallet's own
   balance, history, and future coin selection. Rebuilt on
   getDestForAddress(), which already handles bech32 / script_address /
   script_address2 / P2PKH correctly (it is what addressToScripthash and
   _createRawFundedTransactionElectrum already use).

4. THE SCRIPTHASH ONE. electrumx.py's scripthash_from_address() checked
   script_address but not script_address2. LTC mints P2SH under a second,
   newer version byte after deprecating the one it shares with Bitcoin; an
   LTC P2SH address using it fell through to the bech32-witness branch --
   a plausible-looking but wrong scripthash, not an error. BTCInterface's
   own getDestForAddress() already checks both bytes; this function now
   does too.

5. THE STALE-LABEL ONE. basicswap.py's _computeElectrumLegacyFundsInfo
   flagged every non-bech32 balance as "legacy funds needing
   consolidation". True before PATCH-3 (electrum wallets were P2WPKH-only,
   so non-bech32 could only mean stray funds); false now, for a coin the
   host explicitly adopted at address_type="p2pkh" -- that IS the wallet's
   intended shape. Left unfixed, this is the exact "Fund from wallet" /
   consolidation nudge from earlier in this integration, now firing on a
   wallet that no longer needs it. Skipped when the coin is adopted as
   p2pkh; unchanged otherwise.

None of this enables swapping FROM a purely legacy-derivation wallet -- (1)
is a refusal, not a workaround, because the protocol requirement is real
(see PwndaWalletVault/wiki/synthesis/pwnda-basicswap-convergence-plan.md
and the REU26 ResearchWiki's chain-A lock analysis). It closes the gap
between "silently unsafe or silently wrong" and "cleanly refused or
cleanly correct" for everything this patch touches. Swap participation
from a legacy-only wallet remains future work, gated on giving the wallet
a second, always-available segwit identity to fund and receive a lock
through -- a larger design than a patch series should carry piecemeal.

